  "notes": "6-channel headphone mixing and distribution amplifier (19\" rack, IEC mains). Main stereo input on XLR or 6.35 mm TRS, passed through to MAIN OUT (XLR and TRS). Per channel: DIRECT IN (replaces the main signal), AUX IN (blended with BALANCE), front PHONES OUT and a rear OUT that mirrors it. XLR genders follow the usual convention (not stated). Controls from the Quick Start Guide (HA8000/HA6000): MASTER LEVEL for the MAIN input, per channel OUTPUT LEVEL, L/R MONO, BALANCE (MAIN/DIRECT against AUX IN; stereo balance when AUX IN is empty), BASS and TREBLE, and POWER. As the guide states, a cable in a channel's DIRECT IN mutes the MAIN signal on that channel; MAIN OUT passes the MAIN input straight through. Assumption: levels at MIN are silent.",
